WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:07.545
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Sunday, October twenty-fifth.

2
00:00:07.545 --> 00:00:12.150
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:20.456
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:20.456 --> 00:00:21.507
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:21.507 --> 00:00:30.649
Riyadh's main airport reopens today after two weeks shut, with fresh missile and drone intercepts this morning.

6
00:00:30.649 --> 00:00:36.543
Iran claims it downed a US drone over Bandar Abbas.

7
00:00:36.543 --> 00:00:38.917
Crimea remains on rolling blackouts.

8
00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:44.590
Here's the detail.

9
00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:47.220
What changed.

10
00:00:47.220 --> 00:01:02.524
King Khalid International Airport in Riyadh said late Saturday both terminals reopen today: terminal one for domestic flights, terminal two for international flights by Saudi carriers only, Al Arabiya reports.

11
00:01:02.524 --> 00:01:15.207
The airport had been closed since October tenth after a Houthi attack that Al Jazeera reports killed thirteen people.

12
00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:30.896
This morning the Saudi-led coalition says it intercepted a Houthi ballistic missile and a drone aimed at the Riyadh area, then ten more ballistic missiles toward the south.

13
00:01:30.896 --> 00:01:37.551
A Houthi spokesman said the Riyadh airport remains a target.

14
00:01:37.551 --> 00:01:46.237
Status: reopening and intercepts confirmed by Saudi officials; the airport threat is the group's own statement.

15
00:01:46.237 --> 00:01:57.914
If you have travelers routing through Riyadh, confirm the booking with the carrier and keep a fallback route.

16
00:01:57.914 --> 00:02:09.448
In Iran, the army says it shot down a US LUCAS drone over Bandar Abbas this morning, Reuters reports, citing Tasnim.

17
00:02:09.448 --> 00:02:10.353
Status: Iran's claim only.

18
00:02:10.353 --> 00:02:14.104
No US confirmation.

19
00:02:14.104 --> 00:02:18.702
Bandar Abbas sits on the Strait of Hormuz.

20
00:02:18.702 --> 00:02:25.831
In occupied Crimea, the power cut that began Friday night continues.

21
00:02:25.831 --> 00:02:35.489
Sevastopol moved to rolling blackouts this morning, Russian state media report, with districts taking turns for power.

22
00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:48.662
The Russian-installed energy company says limits remain across the peninsula, with no date for full restoration.

23
00:02:48.662 --> 00:02:51.552
Status: reported by Russian-installed officials.

24
00:02:51.552 --> 00:03:01.860
If you have people there, treat power and mobile signal as intermittent and keep devices charged.

25
00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.384
Operations check.

26
00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:07.640
Airspace: Riyadh as above.

27
00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:20.431
Saudi civil defense also reported falling debris in the Mecca and Medina regions Saturday after two Houthi missile intercepts; the Houthis deny targeting either city.

28
00:03:20.431 --> 00:03:24.804
Shipping: no new ship attacks in this window.

29
00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:40.151
The latest UK Maritime Trade Operations warning, from Thursday, is a tanker hit by an unknown projectile in the Strait of Hormuz; the ship continued.

30
00:03:40.151 --> 00:03:53.859
Internet and telecom: Sevastopol officials say about forty percent of mobile base stations are working, with about four hours of backup power at those sites.

31
00:03:53.859 --> 00:03:59.372
No fresh network data on Crimea since Saturday.

32
00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:02.571
Power: Crimea as above.

33
00:04:02.571 --> 00:04:06.758
Borders: no new country-wide closures.

34
00:04:06.758 --> 00:04:15.741
Hazards: Typhoon Champi has weakened and is turning northeast off China's Zhejiang coast toward southwestern Japan.

35
00:04:15.741 --> 00:04:29.563
A deep magnitude seven quake near Japan's Bonin Islands last night brought no tsunami threat, US tsunami centers say.

36
00:04:29.563 --> 00:04:30.498
That's today's brief.

37
00:04:30.498 --> 00:04:35.954
Current as of seven forty-five a.m.

38
00:04:35.954 --> 00:04:36.454
Central, Sunday.

39
00:04:36.454 --> 00:04:41.414
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

40
00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:46.266
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

41
00:04:46.266 --> 00:04:50.932
Check the original source before you act.

42
00:04:50.932 --> 00:04:53.167
Questions?

43
00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:56.464
Reach Tueri at contact at tuerisystems dot com.

44
00:04:56.464 --> 00:05:01.342
Thanks for listening.
